# Copy to ~/.mayo-watchdog.env ON THE MINI, fill in, chmod 600.
# NEVER commit the real file — it is outside the repo on purpose.
#
# Getting the two values:
#   1. Talk to @BotFather on Telegram -> /newbot -> it gives you the token.
#   2. Send any message to your new bot, then:
#      curl -s "https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates" | grep -o '"id":[0-9-]*'
#      The chat id is the one in the "chat" object (negative for groups).

TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<from @BotFather>
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=<your chat id>

# --- optional overrides ---------------------------------------------------
# Alert above this % used on /
# DISK_PCT_MAX=85
# Alert below this % system-wide free memory
# MEM_FREE_PCT_MIN=15
# Alert above this % of a container's own memory limit
# CONTAINER_MEM_PCT_MAX=90
# While a check stays broken, re-notify at most this often (hours)
# REPEAT_HOURS=6
# Where the ELK stack lives (for the Elasticsearch health check)
# ELK_DIR=$HOME/elk-stage
